+## Key Capabilities
 
-## 📦 Installation
+- **Read and traverse Microsoft OneNote (.one) files in Python** - Navigate document content and its child nodes. Available through the public `DocumentVisitor`, `Node`, and `Document` APIs.
+- **Access OneNote pages and page titles** - Inspect page content together with its title information. Available through the public `Node`, `Page`, and `Title` APIs.
+- **Extract rich text and formatting from OneNote files** - Access text and its formatting data. Available through the public `TextRun`, `RichText`, and `TextStyle` APIs.
+- **Extract images and attached files from OneNote files** - Retrieve embedded images and attached-file content. Available through the public `AttachedFile` and `Image` APIs.
+- **Read OneNote tables, rows, and cells** - Traverse tables, rows, and cells. Available through the public `TableRow`, `TableCell`, and `Table` APIs.
+- **Inspect tags in OneNote documents** - Inspect tags on content nodes. Available through the public `NoteTag` and `Node` APIs.
+- **Read numbered lists and outline elements in OneNote documents** - Inspect numbered lists and outline structures. Available through the public `NumberList`, `OutlineElement`, and `Outline` APIs.
+- **Export PDF files** - Create files in the listed output formats.
 
